/* Copyright 2026 Rhett Creighton - Apache License 2.0
 *
 * flags — the CLOSED catalog of every runtime/build/test flag and Makefile
 * variable this tree reads out of its process environment. A name that is
 * not written down here is not a flag: `check-flag-registry` refuses a
 * `getenv("ZCL_...")` call or a shell/Makefile `${ZCL_...}` read whose name
 * is not a row in this file, and refuses a row this file still carries once
 * nothing in the tree reads it any more. The set can only shrink on
 * purpose.
 *
 * This file is the ONE declaration. The gate that enforces it:
 *
 *   tools/lint/lintc/gate_flag_registry.c   parses this file as text and
 *                                           scans the tree for reads
 *   docs/FLAGS.md                          the plain-language explanation
 *
 * Row shape:
 *
 *   Z23_FLAG(name_, kind_, default_, expires_, why_)
 *
 *   name_      the flag's exact spelling, verbatim, e.g. "ZCL_LINT_SERIAL".
 *   kind_      one of four strings:
 *                "env_runtime" — read via getenv() from compiled C at run
 *                                time.
 *                "env_build"   — read by a build/dev-tooling shell script
 *                                (not a test, not a Makefile assignment).
 *                "env_test"    — read by test-harness C or a script under
 *                                a tests/ path.
 *                "make_var"    — read inside the Makefile itself (a
 *                                variable a caller can override with
 *                                `make VAR=... target` or an exported
 *                                shell variable of the same name).
 *   default_   the literal default value if the read site names one
 *              (e.g. "0", "10", a path), else "-".
 *   expires_   "YYYY-MM-DD" the flag must be gone by, or "-" if it never
 *              expires. An expired row fails the gate — remove the flag
 *              and the row together, or push the date out on purpose.
 *   why_       one plain sentence: what decision the flag makes. Rows
 *              produced by the first mechanical sweep of the tree that
 *              found no comment or doc naming the flag say
 *              "undocumented; first use <path>:<line>" instead of
 *              inventing a reason — that string is the debt marker; grep
 *              it to find what still needs a real sentence.
 *
 * Sorted alphabetically by name_. Order carries no meaning beyond that;
 * unlike fleet_vitals.def nothing indexes a flag by its position, so
 * inserting or removing a row is always safe.
 *
 * Adding a flag: add exactly one row here in the same commit that adds the
 * getenv()/${...} read. Removing a flag: delete both the read site and its
 * row in the same commit — a row with no remaining read site fails the gate
 * (shrink-only registry).
 */

